From: Your Name <your.email@example.com>
Date: Wed, 31 Dec 2025 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix quantization to use int8 instead of uint8

The input_zero_point can be negative (e.g., -128), so we need to use
int8 instead of uint8 for quantized features to avoid data loss.

Signed-off-by: Your Name <your.email@example.com>
---
 pymicro_wakeword/microwakeword.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pymicro_wakeword/microwakeword.py b/pymicro_wakeword/microwakeword.py
index 1234567..abcdefg 100644
--- a/pymicro_wakeword/microwakeword.py
+++ b/pymicro_wakeword/microwakeword.py
@@ -193,7 +193,7 @@ class MicroWakeWord(TfLiteWakeWord):
         quant_features = np.round(
             np.concatenate(self._features, axis=1) / self.input_scale
             + self.input_zero_point
-        ).astype(np.uint8)
+        ).astype(np.int8)
 
         # Stride instead of rolling
         self._features.clear()
-- 
2.34.1